 "_comment": "THE LOT SYSTEM on a HAND-AUTHORED road graph. Where lot_lab.json grows its streets from a metro recipe, this level DRAWS them: road.nodes + road.edges are an explicit planar graph, so the nine blocks are a design decision and identical on every run. Two things follow that the generated lab could not give. First, each block is sized to a DISTRICT'S OWN GRAIN (blockGrainFor: residential wants ~88x72, downtown ~224x130, commercial ~136x92) \u2014 lot_lab's 220 m blocks are 48400 m2 against a residential maximum of 38016, so most of its faces were rejected as unreachable and the map came back nearly empty. Second, road.city_hubs zones the map by hand: a generated net leaves hubs behind for the zoner, an authored one had none, so every block came back residential and the whole city built one program. Non-uniform spacing is the point \u2014 a uniform grid gives one block size and therefore one building.",
